Presented at FASAL-14, Stony Brook University, April 2024. 
Argues that Bengali scrambling involves both A- and A'-movement, with the type determined by the landing site: A'-movement is possible only when Spec,CP is available, and otherwise movement is A-movement. The findings support a position-based account of the A/A' distinction (Keine 2018).

